      "content": "1|Vivacious and charming, Humperdink is a NG dhampir (offspring of a vampire and human) in his early thirties. A snappy dresser, Hump adorns his lanky frame with dark purples and maroons to compliment his pale complexion and shock of red hair. For the purposes of combat, he has levels in warlock and fighter, with a dip into wizard for basic spells like [shield](https://www.dndbeyond.com/spells/2247-shield). Humperdink ascribes to a polyamorous lifestyle, finding attraction in anyone who shares his lust for life. He is also a member of the Order of the Pink Ribbon, a collection of lycanthropes, vampires, and other flesh-eaters who have sworn off eating humanoid or humanoid-derived products.\n2|\n3|### Humperdink’s Laboratory\n4|\n5|A chaotically organized room, [Humperdink’s](https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/hgtmh1/the-loot-tavern#Humperdink) laboratory never has less than half a dozen experiments being simultaneously conducted. Iridescent organs and biostatically preserved creatures line shelves, floating in glowing, colourful liquids. Desks are covered in papers with a mix of arcane runes, scribbled notes, and the mustard stains of hastily eaten blood-sausage sandwiches. Novel biomantic constructs like Poggle, Humperdink’s homunculus helper, or Feviline, the [[The Loot Tavern]]’s cat, explore the dangerous lands under his desk and high up on the shelves.\n6|\n7|**_Services: Spell Scrolls._** Humperdink sells [spell scrolls](https://www.dndbeyond.com/magic-items/5418-spell-scroll). He also carries a variety of _scrolls_ from other schools of magic. To determine his inventory, whenever a creature asks if a _scroll_ is available, roll a **d10**. Humperdink has a number of that _spell scroll_ available for purchase equal to the result of the roll minus the level of the spell. Being a student of the school of biomancy, he always has at least one of each biomancy spell in his inventory available for purchase.\n8|\n9|Number of scrolls available* = d10 - level of spell scroll\n10|\n11|_*Minimum of 1, if biomancy spell._\n12|\n13|If the result is 0 or lower, he doesn’t have the _scroll_, and will gladly buy up to **1d4** of them for one-half of their sale value. This inventory changes periodically (GM’s discretion). The price of _spell scrolls_ is as follows:\n14|\n15||Spell Scroll Level|Rarity|Value|\n16||---|---|---|\n17||[0 (cantrip)](https://www.dndbeyond.com/magic-items/4758-spell-scroll-0-cantrip)|Common|10 gp|\n18||[1](https://www.dndbeyond.com/magic-items/5161-spell-scroll-1st-level)|Common|60 gp|\n19||[2](https://www.dndbeyond.com/magic-items/5162-spell-scroll-2nd-level)|Uncommon|150 gp|\n20||[3](https://www.dndbeyond.com/magic-items/5163-spell-scroll-3rd-level)|Uncommon|300 gp|\n21||[4](https://www.dndbeyond.com/magic-items/5164-spell-scroll-4th-level)|Rare|600 gp|\n22||[5](https://www.dndbeyond.com/magic-items/5165-spell-scroll-5th-level)|Rare|1,200 gp|\n23||[6](https://www.dndbeyond.com/magic-items/5166-spell-scroll-6th-level)|Very rare|3,100 gp|\n24||[7](https://www.dndbeyond.com/magic-items/5167-spell-scroll-7th-level)|Very rare|6,200 gp|\n25||[8](https://www.dndbeyond.com/magic-items/5168-spell-scroll-8th-level)|Very rare|9,300 gp|\n26||[9](https://www.dndbeyond.com/magic-items/5169-spell-scroll-9th-level)|Legendary|19,500 gp|",
